  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/bfd86c83e594946713f14cbdcc9c2dded3b186f9</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/mansourvery-hub/CompreDef/commit/bfd86c83e594946713f14cbdcc9c2dded3b186f9"/>
    <title>
        Merge Yomitan single-best-definition (/termEntries) into master after…
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-05T00:32:20Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323373735?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>mansourvery-hub</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/mansourvery-hub</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Merge Yomitan single-best-definition (/termEntries) into master after live verification

Verified live against Yomitan 26.8.24.0 (Chrome 151, browser-launched
keepalive bridge): fetch now queries POST /termEntries and splits the
response into one DictionaryEntry per dictionary definition, so the
ladder scores each and returns only the winner — 食べる returned 4 split
entries (小学館 8.5k / 大辞林 3.8k / 大辞泉 14.3k / 漢検 284 chars) instead
of /ankiFields&amp;#39; single 61,258-char all-dictionaries glued blob.

- /ankiFields remains as fallback for kanji lookups (口 -&amp;gt; 8 entries).
- Bridge-level error dicts (502) fail fast, no extra round-trips.
- Reading filter applied at headword level; headword term used as entry word.
- Anki-side timeout 10s, nested above bridge&amp;#39;s 8s Yomitan wait.

Local users are unaffected: LocalSQLiteProvider path unchanged; this only
changes what the Yomitan source/fail-safe fetches.

Suite: 208/208 green (incl. new bridge keepalive + anti-zombie guards).&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
