  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/6c997955d68655a81fb01901c43a65bf3871c73f</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/mansourvery-hub/CompreDef/commit/6c997955d68655a81fb01901c43a65bf3871c73f"/>
    <title>
        Fix Yomitan bridge MV3 service-worker death: keepalive + anti-zombie …
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-05T00:24:25Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/323373735?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>mansourvery-hub</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/mansourvery-hub</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Fix Yomitan bridge MV3 service-worker death: keepalive + anti-zombie self-heal

Root cause (verified live, Chrome 151 + Yomitan 26.8.24.0): Yomitan&amp;#39;s MV3
service worker owns the native-messaging port. ~30s after connectNative the
SW suspends, Chrome closes both pipes, and the old host turned into a zombie:
still holding port 19633 with stdin dead, so every /ankiFields returned 502
forever and no new launch could bind. This reproduced every Chrome restart
and was the real &amp;#39;Yomitan completely dead&amp;#39; incident.

Fixes bundled in BRIDGE_SCRIPT:
- Keepalive thread pings the port every 20s; receiving a message resets the
  SW&amp;#39;s 30s idle timer (Chrome 105/110/114 lifecycle rules), keeping the SW
  and port alive for as long as Chrome runs.
- Stdin reader thread owns stdin; on EOF (SW suspended/browser quit) it
  fails pending requests and shuts the host down, so the process exits and
  frees port 19633 for the next launch (anti-zombie self-heal).
- Nonce pairing (_cd in params, echoed by Yomitan) so keepalive echoes and
  stale replies can never mis-pair with a real request&amp;#39;s reply.
- ThreadingHTTPServer: slow Yomitan lookups no longer block other requests.
- YOMITAN_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT 2.0 -&amp;gt; 8.0s (cold first query legitimately takes
  seconds; Anki-side 10s stays nested above it).

Also:
- Restore _is_browser_launched guard in the installer&amp;#39;s standalone-killer
  (v1.0.34 incident: killer matched yomitan_api.py alone and murdered a
  live browser connection). Zombie browser-launched hosts are now left to
  the crowbar takeover, never killed by us.
- Regression suite made hermetic: aqt stub now returns yomitan_fallback:False
  so tests expecting None don&amp;#39;t query a live Yomitan on dev machines.
- New test_yomitan_bridge_sw_keepalive: 17 checks guarding keepalive
  interval &amp;lt;30s, reader-thread shutdown chain, nonce pairing, browser-launched
  guard, and nested timeouts.

Live-verified: /ankiFields(口) rich HTML after full chain; 5-minute idle
soak with yomitanVersion green at every minute; bridge self-exits within 1s
of Chrome death, freeing the port; /termEntries splits 食べる into 4
per-dictionary entries (8.5k/3.8k/14.3k/284 chars) vs the old 61,258-char
glued blob, ladder returns single best.

Suite: 208/208 green.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
